.pytest_cache/

# OneDrive sync duplicates: "foo(1).py", "foo(2).yaml", etc.
# OneDrive recreates these on every sync when it sees a collision.
# They are never imported or referenced; they shadow real modules when
# Python resolves an import against a stale __pycache__ entry.
*(*[0-9]).*
*(*[0-9])/
*(*[0-9])
# ...and everything inside a directory OneDrive renamed wholesale.
*(*[0-9])_*/
# Quarantine area holding those artifacts, pending review.
_quarantine_onedrive_duplicates/

# OneDrive internals
.ano/
*.lnk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

checkpoints/
wandb/
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
.env
*.log
.DS_Store

